  "finalAnswerPreview": "## Answer\\n\\nI inspected the workspace, the pinned dependency artifacts, and the local docs before deciding. Result: the cursor is fully determined by the pinned Ordarium artifacts (1.3.1); no peer escalation is warranted. Details below.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 1. What \\\"incremental state-observation cursor\\\" is here\\n\\nIt is the change-feed cursor of Ordarium's management-state kind (ORD-BOOT-0), i.e. `StateChangePage.cursor` returned by:\\n\\n- `OperationLedger.changes(filter?: StateChangeFilter, cursor?: string): Promise<StateChangePage>` (optional capability `LedgerCapabilities.stateChangeFeed`)\\n- surfaced through `OrdariumStateStore.changes(...)`\\n\\nEvidence:\\n- `node_modules/@ordarium/core/dist/src/types.d.ts` — `StateChangeFilter`, `StateChangePage`, `StateChangeFeed`, `LedgerCapabilities.stateChangeFeed`; doc text: *\\\"Incremental observation of committed state revisions after a durable position (ORD-BOOT-0)\\\"*.\\n- `node_modules/@ordarium/core/dist/src/state.js` — `createStateStore(...).changes` delegates and fails closed with `LEDGER_CAPABILITY_REQUIRED` via `supportsStateChangeFeed`.\\n- `node_modules/@ordarium/ledger-sqlite/dist/src/index.js` — `SqliteLedger.changes` (~L382–419).\\n- ",
